{
  "category": "Mole Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "A team of DIGLETT triplets. It triggers huge earthquakes by burrowing 60 miles underground.",
      "version": "red"
    },
    {
      "text": "A team of DIGLETT triplets. It triggers huge earthquakes by burrowing 60 miles underground.",
      "version": "blue"
    },
    {
      "text": "A team of triplets that can burrow over 60 MPH. Due to this, some people think it's an earthquake.",
      "version": "yellow"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its three heads bob separately up and down to loosen the soil nearby, making it easier for it to burrow.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "Extremely powerful, they can DIG through even the hardest ground to a depth of over 60 miles.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "These DIGLETT triplets dig over 60 miles below sea level. No one knows what it's like underground.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "DUGTRIO are actually triplets that emerged from one body. As a result, each triplet thinks exactly like the other two triplets. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "DUGTRIO are actually triplets that emerged from one body. As a result, each triplet thinks exactly like the other two triplets. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the triplets originally split from one body, they think exactly alike. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly through the ground.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "In battle, it digs through the ground and strikes the unsuspecting foe from an unexpected direction.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "A team of DIGLETT triplets. It triggers huge earthquakes by burrowing 60 miles underground.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its three heads move alternately, driving it through tough soil to depths of over 60 miles.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its three heads move alternately, driving it through tough soil to depths of over 60 miles.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
