    {
      "text": "In battle, it digs through the ground and strikes the unsuspecting foe from an unexpected direction.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "Extremely powerful, they can dig through even the hardest ground to a depth of over 60 miles.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dugtrio are actually triplets that emerged from one body. As a result, each triplet thinks exactly like the other two triplets. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dugtrio are actually triplets that emerged from one body. As a result, each triplet thinks exactly like the other two triplets. They work cooperatively to burrow endlessly.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "This set of triplets moves cooperatively. It’s the power of teamwork that enables this Pokémon to dig to a depth of 60 miles.",
      "version": "sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Despite the closeness between this Pokémon and farmers and other people, no one has ever seen the parts of it concealed underground.",
      "version": "moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "While the three of them normally get along splendidly, on rare occasions a huge fight will break out over which head gets to eat first.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dugtrio’s heads are sleek and smooth and incredibly hard. It can dig through any soil with its headbutts.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "A team of triplets that can burrow to a depth of 60 miles. It’s reported that this triggers an earthquake.",
      "version": "lets-go-pikachu"
    },
    {
      "text": "A team of triplets that can burrow to a depth of 60 miles. It’s reported that this triggers an earthquake.",
      "version": "lets-go-eevee"
    },
    {
      "text": "A team of Diglett triplets. It triggers huge earthquakes by burrowing 60 miles underground.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "These Diglett triplets dig over 60 miles below sea level. No one knows what it’s like underground.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
